1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,477
Now, what if you pay only the minimum every month?

2
00:00:03,477 --> 00:00:11,819
RBI rules say your loan should not grow if you pay the minimum. So the loan does come down. But very, very slowly.

3
00:00:11,819 --> 00:00:21,171
In the first year, out of every hundred rupees you pay, about seventy four rupees go to interest and GST. Only twenty six rupees cut your loan.

4
00:00:21,171 --> 00:00:29,738
Start with thirty thousand. After one year, you would have paid about twenty thousand. But about twenty four thousand, eight hundred is still pending.

5
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:35,834
After five years? You have paid about seventy thousand. And still about thirteen thousand is pending.

6
00:00:35,834 --> 00:00:39,053
To fully close it, it takes more than ten years.

7
00:00:39,053 --> 00:00:47,254
That is why RBI makes banks print a warning on every bill. If you pay only the minimum, you will keep paying for years.

8
00:00:47,254 --> 00:00:51,460
India now has about eleven point eight six crore credit cards.

9
00:00:51,460 --> 00:01:05,641
As per CRIF High Mark, credit card bills not paid for three months to one year were thirty three thousand, eight hundred and eighty six crore rupees, in March twenty twenty five. That is forty four percent more than the year before.

10
00:01:05,641 --> 00:01:18,541
Forty five percent is too much, right? But in December twenty twenty four, the Supreme Court cancelled an old order that had put a thirty percent limit on credit card interest. So today, no court has put any limit.

11
00:01:18,541 --> 00:01:23,188
So what saves you is not that small number. It is knowing this maths.

12
00:01:23,188 --> 00:01:27,014
Some people use a shortcut. They call it card rotation.

13
00:01:27,014 --> 00:01:34,062
Take money from a friend and pay the full bill. The next day, take the money out of the card as rent, and give it back to the friend.

14
00:01:34,062 --> 00:01:41,239
But your loan does not come down even by one rupee. Only the last date moves to next month. And you pay a fee.

15
00:01:41,239 --> 00:01:49,442
Also, after new RBI rules in twenty twenty five, apps like PhonePe, Paytm and CRED stopped rent payment by credit card.

16
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:55,720
Taking cash from your credit card is even worse. There is a fee, and interest starts from the same day.

17
00:01:55,720 --> 00:02:00,390
So rotation is not a solution. It only pushes the loan to next month.

18
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:03,463
So what should we do? Five simple steps.

19
00:02:03,463 --> 00:02:09,969
One. When you can, pay the full bill. If you set auto pay, set it for the full amount, not the minimum.

20
00:02:09,969 --> 00:02:15,402
Then your card is really free. Up to fifty days interest free, depending on your card.

21
00:02:15,402 --> 00:02:21,194
Two. If you cannot pay the full bill, pay as much as you can. But never less than the minimum.

22
00:02:21,194 --> 00:02:30,511
Because interest on the money you pay stops that day. Pay more, and you pay less interest. And once you clear the full bill, your interest free period comes back.

23
00:02:30,511 --> 00:02:37,349
Three. Till the bill is cleared, keep that card aside. Use UPI or a debit card for daily spending.

24
00:02:37,349 --> 00:02:51,989
Four. If the bill is big, ask your bank to change it into EMI. For example, HDFC's EMI rates are about eleven to twenty five percent. Also check the fee and GST. And never take loans from unknown apps.

25
00:02:51,989 --> 00:03:00,450
Five. If your last date comes before your salary, ask the bank to change your bill date. RBI rules say they must give you this option.

26
00:03:00,450 --> 00:03:08,021
One easy check. On your bill, look for the line called finance charges. If it is not zero, you are paying interest.

27
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:14,175
Remember. The minimum amount saves you from late fees and a bad CIBIL report. Not from interest.

28
00:03:14,175 --> 00:03:23,791
Remember three numbers. Forty five percent interest. Eighteen percent GST on top. And zero interest free days for new spending till the old bill is cleared.

29
00:03:23,791 --> 00:03:29,630
The minimum is like an emergency brake. Use it only in an emergency, not every month.

30
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:34,281
What do you pay every month? The full bill, or the minimum? Tell me in the comments.

31
00:03:34,281 --> 00:03:38,934
In the next video, we will see what happens if you cannot pay even the minimum.

32
00:03:38,934 --> 00:03:45,567
If this helped you, share it with one friend who uses a credit card. Subscribe to the channel. See you soon. Jai Hind.

